  <content>
  <section><title> Cool Down (5 minutes)</title>
<title>Student Activity</title>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>Complete the table with the perimeter of a square for each given side length.</item>
</list>
<table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
 
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>
      side length (inches)
		</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
        perimeter (inches)
      </emphasis></entry></row></thead><tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>0.5</para>
      </entry>
      <entry/>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>7</para>
      </entry>
      <entry/>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>20</para>
      </entry>
      <entry/>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>
<para> <emphasis>Answer: </emphasis> </para>
<table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
 
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>
      side length (inches)
      </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
      perimeter (inches)
      </emphasis></entry></row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>0.5</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>2</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>7</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>28</para>
      </entry>
	  </row></thead><tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>20</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>80</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Write a rule for a function, \(P\), that gives the perimeter of a square in inches when the side length is \(x\) inches.
    
  </item>
  <para> <emphasis>Answer: </emphasis> \(
    P(x)=4x
    \)</para>
  <item>What is the value of \(P(9.1)\)? What does it tell us about the side length and perimeter of the square?</item>
  <para> <emphasis>Answer: </emphasis> \(P(9.1)=36.4\). It tells us that when the side length of the square is 9.1 inches, the perimeter of the square is 36.4 inches.</para>
</list>
</section>
